  "notes": "Flow interrogation log: captures the rationale for each trade (exit/entry/trim) \u2014 populated by interactive runs asking 'why' and by scheduled runs writing 'UNCAPTURED' for manual review. Each entry: {date, ticker, action ('exit'|'trim'|'entry'), qty_change, price_at_trade, reason ('dollar-cost-averaging'|'dca-into-diversification'|'re-entry-after-stop'|'stop-loss'|'thesis-change'|'raise-cash'|'rebalance'|UNCAPTURED, or free text if the user typed something not on that list), notes}. Enables sell-discipline tracking and proposal scoring against actual user behavior. | SEEDED 2026-07-28: back-filled the 07-24 and 07-27 stop-out events (reconstructed, fills approximate) and the 07-28 redeployment (fills exact). G26 now has data for the first time. | 2026-07-29: 'dollar-cost-averaging' promoted from a free-text answer to a full 5th standard reason (see G35, TRADE RATIONALE CAPTURE step 2.9 in SKILL.md) after going 5-for-5 on its first day. Capture is now two AskUserQuestion steps since the tool hard-caps at 4 custom options per question and 5 standing buckets don't fit in one ask. Step 1 is direction-aware (same day, user request): a buy (qty_diff > 0) is asked 'was this DCA?' first, a sell (qty_diff < 0) is asked 'was this a stop-loss?' first; step 2 shows whichever 4 of the 5 reasons step 1 didn't already rule out. | 2026-08-03: 'dca-into-diversification' and 're-entry-after-stop' promoted to standing buy-side reasons (see G45) after both recurred via 'Other' the same day \u2014 a same-day MU stop-loss/rebuy whipsaw pair (re-entry-after-stop) and a five-ticker weekend diversification buy the user confirmed as DCA into diversification. Buy-side step 1 changed shape from a yes/no to a 4-option question (DCA / DCA-into-diversification / Re-entry-after-stop / Something else) to keep 3 buy-relevant reasons within the cap; sell-side step 1 is unchanged. | 2026-08-13 SMITH-LEDGER (G64/G65/G66): first full email reconciliation. 11 rows corrected, 13 rows ADDED (the entire 2026-07-28 redeployment beyond the 4 named clips was absent from trades.json though present in lots.json -- the two files had silently diverged), 1 row split (NVDA 07-27 was two fills, not one), 1 ticker corrected (a 07-28 row recorded as GOOG is in fact GOOGL/Alphabet Class A per ticker_map). Every row now carries price_source ('email_confirmed' = verified against an INDmoney confirmation; 'reconstructed' = rests on a quantity diff and MUST be quarantined from P&L; 'unknown' = no price). ts_utc/order_type/qty_source added where verified. | 2026-08-15 SMITH-LEDGER (this run): 10 rows ADDED for IREN(x2)/BE(x2)/GLW/GEV/VRT/MU/COHR/AMAT fills dated 2026-08-13/08-14 that were missing from trades.json and had triggered a stale ticker-only reason-matching bug in smith_math.py's qty_changes construction (see per-row notes). All 10 are email-confirmed (Amount/Price/Shares/Order Type all read directly, none derived or reconstructed). 9 of 10 are Order Type Market -> reason UNCAPTURED; the AMAT SELL is Order Type stop -> reason stop-loss (genuinely, not inferred).\n\nCORPORATE-ACTION ROWS (added 2026-08-15). A row with no `type` is a plain trade -- every pre-existing row keeps working unchanged. A row with type='corporate_action' records an event that moves or creates shares WITHOUT a buy/sell confirmation, which an email-sourced ledger cannot otherwise see. This is what G68/G71 were missing.\n  {\"date\":\"YYYY-MM-DD\", \"type\":\"corporate_action\", \"ca_type\":<see below>,\n   \"ticker\":\"GOOG\", \"qty_change\":-3.0, \"to_ticker\":\"GOOGL\", \"to_qty\":3.0,\n   \"ratio\":null, \"price_at_trade\":null, \"reason\":\"corporate_action\",\n   \"source\":\"brokerage statement 2026-06\", \"notes\":\"...\"}\nca_type: conversion (moves shares between symbols, CARRIES basis and acquisition date -- the LTCG clock does NOT restart) | split (qty x ratio, per-share basis / ratio, dates preserved) | fractional_credit (shares with no purchase; null price is flagged) | spinoff (source keeps its shares) | adjustment (explicit, sourced reconciliation to broker truth when the cause is genuinely unknown -- recorded rather than force-matched).\n`source` is REQUIRED: this data is not in email, so an unsourced row is unverifiable.\nApply with: python3 scripts/smith_math.py lots --base-dir . [--holdings <run>/holdings.json] [--write] | 2026-08-24 SMITH-LEDGER (run 2026-08-24-0855, QUICK sweep): reconciled the 9 qty_changes flagged by compute_book.json (BE, MRVL, INTC, QCOM, CLS, TER, COHR, IREN, BX) against INDmoney email confirmations for 2026-08-20 through 2026-08-24. All 9 tickers fully accounted for by 10 confirmations dated 2026-08-21 (TER produced two separate sell confirmations 22s apart -> two rows, not one averaged fill, per Hard Rule 3). CLS and TER were flagged likely_corporate_action=true by the compute layer (near-total-to-dust ratios) but VERIFIED as ordinary stop-loss sells: both positions already carried tiny fractional-share dust from earlier 2026-07 fills, which is what made the post-sale residual look corporate-action-shaped. COHR and IREN were full exits (was held, now 0) and BX was a RE-ENTRY into a name fully exited on 2026-08-17 (not a first-ever buy). No rows required correction; all 10 new rows added clean. See individual row notes for detail. | 2026-08-25 SMITH-LEDGER (run 2026-08-25-1357): reconciled the 11 qty_changes flagged by compute_book.json (COHR, NBIS, NVDA, SKHY, KLAC new entries; MRVL, MU, GOOG, CIEN, ASML, AMAT adds) against INDmoney email confirmations dated 2026-08-24T18:26:09Z-18:37:45Z, all Market BUYs, all qty exactly matching the Shares: field (no truncated snippets required a get_thread fallback that changed a number). MU's likely_corporate_action flag (ratio 2.9985) was verified as an ordinary 1-share buy. Separately, while pulling this window's confirmations, found real email confirmations for the 9 stop-loss sells already in trades.json as reconstructed rows dated 2026-08-24 (NVDA, NBIS, SKHY, MRVL, AMAT, BE, GLW, LRCX, MU) from the prior run's 21:07 IST intraday check -- corrected all 9 to email_confirmed prices/order_type per Hard Rule 1/4 (a reconstructed row with a recoverable confirmation should not stay reconstructed). See per-row notes for exact deltas. | 2026-08-26 SMITH-LEDGER (run 2026-08-26-1315, QUICK sweep): reconciled the 10 qty_changes flagged by compute_book.json (AMAT, ASML, CLS, GLW, LRCX, TER adds; LITE, SMCI new entries; MSFT sell; SNDK dust exit) against INDmoney email confirmations dated 2026-08-25T13:39:24Z-14:00:26Z. All 9 real fills are email-confirmed (Amount/Price/Shares/Order Type read directly from get_thread bodies, none derived or reconstructed) -- 9 threads found for 9 expected fills via search_threads, no pagination needed (resultCountEstimate 9). All 9 are Order Type Market. Two flagged likely_corporate_action=true by the compute layer (ASML ratio 2.0, AMAT ratio 1.9919) were VERIFIED as ordinary buys, not splits/CAs -- both artifacts of the base qty already carrying small dust. MSFT SELL + CLS BUY recorded as reason='profit_rotation' (executing live proposals.json pair_id profit_rotation-MSFT-CLS) per orchestrator directive -- tickers/sides/timing all match the pair, though BOTH fill prices diverge materially from the proposal's snapshot prices (CLS -28%, MSFT +11.4%); see data_quality in this run's ledger.md. SNDK's 1e-06sh dust lot closed via a sourced corporate_action/adjustment row (no real trade exists at that quantity)."
}